From: htrecomp
Subject: [PATCH] audio: stop clobbering the guest's XMA output read offset

NOT APPLIED BY DEFAULT. See SDK_PATCHES.md item 4, which marks this
"Unproven": it was written while chasing an audio stutter that turned out to
be timer resolution, and was never independently shown to fix anything. It
survives only because it matches Xenia's ownership model.

The guest owns output_buffer_read_offset via XMASetOutputBufferReadOffset;
copying it back in the merge fights the guest for ownership.

Apply with:
  cd third_party/rexglue-sdk
  git apply ../../patches/0002-OPTIONAL-xma-do-not-clobber-guest-read-offset.patch

Revert first if audio misbehaves on your platform. Note that the proven half
of the original audio fix - timeBeginPeriod(1) in src/main.cpp - is Windows
only, so macOS and Linux audio pacing is untested territory either way.
---
diff --git a/src/audio/xma_context.cpp b/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
index 11b83be..70d8b0f 100644
--- a/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
+++ b/src/audio/xma_context.cpp
@@ -417,7 +417,6 @@ void XmaContext::StoreContextMerged(const XMA_CONTEXT_DATA& data,
   fresh.input_buffer_read_offset = data.input_buffer_read_offset;
   fresh.error_status = data.error_status;
   fresh.current_buffer = data.current_buffer;
-  fresh.output_buffer_read_offset = data.output_buffer_read_offset;
 
   fresh.Store(context_ptr);
 }
